module repro_acp.output_over_4k

// Oracle 0.1.0 / `nova test` on Windows: a test binary prints one line per test, "  PASS: <name>". A binary whose lines come to more than 4096 bytes
// (the Windows pipe buffer) blocks on its stdout until someone reads the pipe. `nova test` on ONE unit reads it in time. `nova test <dir>` over
// several units that run together (the default is as many jobs as CPUs) did not read it, and the binary was killed by the limit of
// about 70 s: "TIMEOUT <unit> # killed after 70000ms", with a binary that was idle (no CPU, no children). Run this folder together with
// other units, e.g. `cd spikes/env/repro_acp; nova test src` (the other repro folders there fail to compile, that is their point; copy
// this folder next to two or three healthy units to see the timeout), or start the binary by hand with its stdout piped and unread.
// The ACP tests of the product are split in several units whose lines stay under 4096 bytes each, and test names are kept short.
// Expected: PASS in every case. Actual: TIMEOUT when several units run together.

test "output filler number 01, a test name of about one hundred characters long, to make the output of the unit big" {
    assert(true)
}

test "output filler number 02, a test name of about one hundred characters long, to make the output of the unit big" {
    assert(true)
}

